      "status": "answer",
      "answer": "An LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) network retains sequence information through its unique architecture, which includes memory cells and gating mechanisms. The memory cells store information over long periods, while the gates (input, output, and forget gates) control the flow of information. The input gate determines what information to add to the cell state, the forget gate decides what to discard, and the output gate controls what information to send to the next layer. This structure allows LSTMs to effectively learn from sequences and maintain context over time, making them particularly useful for tasks involving sequential data, such as time series prediction or natural language processing.",
